      "summary": "Migration 0041 adds two tenant tables (tenant_id in every key, ENABLE and FORCE RLS with tenant_fence, insert-only trigger, CHECKs on every enum, empty tools, SELECT and INSERT to impact_app only) and a nullable tenant-keyed policy pin on ai_advisory_request; 0001-0040 unchanged (TH01, TH10: native fence and role tests). The contract makes policy_version required on AIAdvisoryRequest (old clients get 422) and closes AIPolicyCommand (TH03). The access policy adds ai.policy.manage for TENANT_ADMIN with 300-second fresh assurance; the initial-access profile hash changes, so existing tenants need the reviewed ceiling widening before holding it (TH35). The gate runs before any reservation or provider call (TH34, TH35); tools are refused in the API and the database (TH21, TH33); attempts stay three per day (TH24). New residuals: no destination is approved, so TH34 is BLOCK (keep the server switch off for real data); a policy change after a reservation does not stop that one in-flight call (TH35).",
